      "text/html": [
       "<div style=\"color:#6b7280;font-size:0.9em\">Context: tables imba.order_products, imba.aisles, imba.orders, imba.products, imba.departments, employees · 3 example(s)</div>"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.HTML object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/html": [
       "<details style=\"color:#6b7280;\"><summary><b>Thinking</b></summary><pre style=\"white-space:pre-wrap;color:#6b7280;\">I need to write a single SQL query that identifies the top 10 most popular products based on the number of times they were ordered.\n",
       "\n",
       "1.  **Identify the relevant table:** `imba.order_products` contains records of products in orders (`product_id`).\n",
       "2.  **Count occurrences:** I need to count how many times each `product_id` appears in `imba.order_products`.\n",
       "3.  **Join for names:** I need to join with `imba.products` to get the `product_name`.\n",
       "4.  **Group and Order:** Group by `product_id` and `product_name`, order by the count descending, and limit to 10.\n",
       "\n",
       "Steps:\n",
       "1.  CTE/Subquery to count product occurrences: `SELECT product_id, COUNT(*) AS times_ordered FROM imba.order_products GROUP BY product_id`.\n",
       "2.  Join this result with `imba.products` on `product_id`.\n",
       "3.  Select `product_name` and `times_ordered`.\n",
       "4.  Order by `times_ordered` DESC and limit 10.\n",
       "\n",
       "This structure is similar to the first example provided in the prompt.</pre></details>"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.HTML object>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "text/markdown": [
       "### SQL\n",
       "```sql\n",
       "SELECT\n",
       "  p.product_name,\n",
       "  t.times_ordered\n",
       "FROM (\n",
       "  SELECT\n",
       "    product_id,\n",
       "    COUNT(*) AS times_ordered\n",
       "  FROM imba.order_products\n",
       "  GROUP BY\n",
       "    product_id\n",
       ") AS t\n",
       "JOIN imba.products AS p\n",
       "  ON t.product_id = p.product_id\n",
       "ORDER BY\n",
       "  t.times_ordered DESC\n",
       "LIMIT 10;\n",
       "```"
      ],
      "text/plain": [
       "<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"
      ]
